WEBVTT

1
00:00:29,564 --> 00:00:31,465
(creaking)

2
00:00:38,907 --> 00:00:40,575
(wind whistling)

3
00:00:40,675 --> 00:00:42,644
(water lapping)

4
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:45,813
(gull cries)

5
00:00:55,489 --> 00:00:57,057
(creaking)

6
00:00:58,793 --> 00:01:00,595
(water rippling, gull squawks)

7
00:01:07,802 --> 00:01:09,469
(engine rumbling)

8
00:01:15,677 --> 00:01:17,579
(tyres crunching)

9
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:21,081
(handbrake clicks, engine cuts)

10
00:01:26,688 --> 00:01:27,822
(car door opens)

11
00:01:28,957 --> 00:01:30,625
(wind howling)

12
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:41,234
(gate, chains clanking)

13
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:05,560
(wind whistling, creaking)

14
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,567
Jesus Christ!

15
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,772
(creaking)

16
00:02:59,312 --> 00:03:01,381
(dripping)

17
00:03:36,349 --> 00:03:38,251
She's back.

18
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,855
(slow dramatic music)

19
00:03:43,891 --> 00:03:45,560
(birds singing)

20
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:00,474
(dogs barking)

21
00:04:16,724 --> 00:04:18,659
(youth shouting)

22
00:04:50,158 --> 00:04:51,826
(clock ticking)

23
00:05:10,611 --> 00:05:13,080
I know 'tis hard but...

24
00:05:16,651 --> 00:05:19,352
we've gotta decide what to do.

25
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:34,434
Tina?

26
00:05:48,249 --> 00:05:50,350
(slow dramatic music)
(grass rustling)

27
00:05:54,922 --> 00:05:56,924
(heavy breathing)

28
00:05:59,994 --> 00:06:01,896
(dog barking distantly)

29
00:06:12,506 --> 00:06:14,542
(leaves rustling)

30
00:06:16,811 --> 00:06:18,846
(slow dramatic music continues)

31
00:06:25,119 --> 00:06:26,821
(birds squawking)

32
00:06:35,529 --> 00:06:37,565
(seagulls crying)

33
00:07:06,327 --> 00:07:08,029
(van rumbling loudly)

34
00:07:14,702 --> 00:07:16,704
(melancholic music)

35
00:07:40,127 --> 00:07:42,495
(waves crashing)

36
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:44,966
(whooshing)

37
00:08:28,609 --> 00:08:30,044
Mr Richards?

38
00:08:30,778 --> 00:08:33,047
(thunder cracks, rain pouring)

39
00:08:37,051 --> 00:08:38,019
Emily?

40
00:08:41,288 --> 00:08:42,523
What?

41
00:08:44,291 --> 00:08:45,960
Oh, Mrs Richards!

42
00:08:48,195 --> 00:08:49,730
Come on. Let's get you in.

43
00:08:54,935 --> 00:08:56,070
Okay?

44
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:57,738
(rain clanking on gutter)

45
00:08:58,507 --> 00:08:59,874
(music tinkling)

46
00:09:01,575 --> 00:09:03,010
TELEVISION: <i>Hello there.</i>

47
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:04,478
<i>How are you today?</i>

48
00:09:04,578 --> 00:09:07,014
<i>I hope you're feeling</i>
<i>super-duper.</i>

49
00:09:07,148 --> 00:09:08,282
<i>I know I am.</i>

50
00:09:08,382 --> 00:09:09,583
<i>Do you know why?</i>

51
00:09:09,683 --> 00:09:11,152
<i>Because...</i>

52
00:09:11,252 --> 00:09:12,887
<i>it's making time!</i>

53
00:09:12,987 --> 00:09:15,189
<i>It's my favourite time</i>
<i>of the week.</i>

54
00:09:15,289 --> 00:09:16,924
(water dripping)

55
00:09:19,427 --> 00:09:20,895
(clanking)

56
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,268
(louder dripping)

57
00:09:30,838 --> 00:09:32,306
(Mrs Richards sighs)

58
00:09:33,974 --> 00:09:36,143
(television continues playing)
(stool scrapes)

59
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:11,011
Hark...

60
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:14,815
My boy's coming home.

61
00:10:16,484 --> 00:10:18,185
(dark music)

62
00:10:25,159 --> 00:10:26,794
(heavy rain)

63
00:10:34,935 --> 00:10:38,038
MIKE: So, we gonna try again?

64
00:10:40,575 --> 00:10:42,143
(creaking)

65
00:10:48,617 --> 00:10:49,850
Are we?

66
00:10:55,524 --> 00:10:56,924
(rain pattering)

67
00:10:57,758 --> 00:10:59,293
(creaking)

68
00:11:02,531 --> 00:11:04,098
(suspenseful music)

69
00:11:09,937 --> 00:11:12,072
We keep this between us.

70
00:11:15,276 --> 00:11:16,443
Who's gonna crew?

71
00:11:20,615 --> 00:11:22,416
There ent no-one left here,
Mike.

72
00:11:23,518 --> 00:11:24,885
(torrential rain)

73
00:11:46,508 --> 00:11:48,042
(drip gets faster)

74
00:11:49,009 --> 00:11:50,778
(rain pattering hard)

75
00:11:52,514 --> 00:11:53,682
Sorry!

76
00:11:53,781 --> 00:11:55,182
(pouring)

77
00:11:55,282 --> 00:11:56,717
(television continues)

78
00:12:20,908 --> 00:12:22,343
(ominous music)
(door bangs)

79
00:12:23,077 --> 00:12:24,211
(splash)

80
00:12:25,714 --> 00:12:26,880
EMILY: There he is.

81
00:12:27,214 --> 00:12:28,415
(splosh)

82
00:12:28,717 --> 00:12:30,184
Right, Mrs Richards.

83
00:12:30,384 --> 00:12:31,885
Nick'll take you home.

84
00:12:33,053 --> 00:12:34,822
(Mrs Richard groans)

85
00:12:38,759 --> 00:12:40,494
(rain pouring outside)

86
00:12:44,566 --> 00:12:46,000
(thunder rumbles)

87
00:13:10,525 --> 00:13:13,160
(footsteps receding quietly)

88
00:13:16,731 --> 00:13:18,465
(clock ticking)

89
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:42,557
She d'get the past and present
mixed up.

90
00:13:48,262 --> 00:13:50,331
They caught some fish that day.

91
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:58,172
Different place this was
back then.

92
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,577
Harbour full of boats,
trucks, men.

93
00:14:03,812 --> 00:14:05,212
Fulla life.

94
00:14:11,686 --> 00:14:13,987
Three year Luke
was on that boat.

95
00:14:18,827 --> 00:14:20,361
He never went again.

96
00:14:25,099 --> 00:14:27,468
Guilt's hard shadow
to live under.

97
00:14:38,178 --> 00:14:40,414
(clock ticking intensifies)

98
00:14:47,722 --> 00:14:49,089
Will you be okay?

99
00:14:49,624 --> 00:14:52,459
S'long as sun come up 'morra,
we'll be okay.

100
00:14:54,094 --> 00:14:55,929
No good lookin' back, boy.

101
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,969
(rain pouring)

102
00:15:05,372 --> 00:15:06,574
(door closes)

103
00:15:07,842 --> 00:15:09,943
(boat creaking)

104
00:15:30,799 --> 00:15:32,600
(water lapping gently)

105
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:08,536
MURGEY: Excuse me, Sir!

106
00:16:19,379 --> 00:16:20,548
Sir!

107
00:16:20,682 --> 00:16:22,115
(rain pouring)

108
00:16:27,454 --> 00:16:28,656
Need a skipper?

109
00:16:29,824 --> 00:16:31,158
Oo's askin'?

110
00:16:31,793 --> 00:16:32,694
I am.

111
00:16:35,563 --> 00:16:36,631
Do I know ya?

112
00:16:37,532 --> 00:16:38,432
Do ya?

113
00:16:41,335 --> 00:16:42,436
Maybe.

114
00:16:43,972 --> 00:16:45,573
(low rumbling)

115
00:16:51,746 --> 00:16:53,046
(baby gurgles)

116
00:16:56,584 --> 00:16:58,118
What was Alan like?

117
00:17:01,154 --> 00:17:02,489
Free-spirited.

118
00:17:06,661 --> 00:17:08,262
Or if you're looking out
the other window,

119
00:17:08,362 --> 00:17:09,797
a bloody coward who spent
his life

120
00:17:09,898 --> 00:17:11,164
runnin' away.

121
00:17:23,377 --> 00:17:24,779
He had his moments, though.

122
00:17:30,183 --> 00:17:32,419
He'd have loved you
so much, Linsey.

123
00:17:36,524 --> 00:17:37,659
(slurping)

124
00:17:37,759 --> 00:17:39,226
(rock music playing)

125
00:17:43,063 --> 00:17:44,398
(door closes)

126
00:17:47,936 --> 00:17:50,505
-MIKE: Hiya, Jess.
-Alright?

127
00:17:51,639 --> 00:17:53,307
Got summin' for yer.

128
00:17:55,910 --> 00:17:57,579
It was your dad's.

129
00:17:58,345 --> 00:18:00,247
Found it in some stuff

130
00:18:00,815 --> 00:18:02,282
from back along.

131
00:18:09,057 --> 00:18:10,457
Suits ya.

132
00:18:14,494 --> 00:18:15,730
Mm...

133
00:18:15,830 --> 00:18:16,798
Okay.

134
00:18:19,067 --> 00:18:20,768
(music playing faintly)

135
00:18:49,964 --> 00:18:51,131
Okay?

136
00:18:59,306 --> 00:19:00,842
(creaking, clanking)

137
00:19:03,745 --> 00:19:05,613
(clanking)

138
00:19:07,949 --> 00:19:10,217
(clanging)

139
00:19:13,988 --> 00:19:14,856
(bang)

140
00:19:15,123 --> 00:19:16,189
(small thud)

141
00:19:19,694 --> 00:19:20,795
(metal scraping)

142
00:19:26,601 --> 00:19:28,235
(big splash)

143
00:19:45,987 --> 00:19:47,320
Wasson?

144
00:19:51,059 --> 00:19:52,325
(sniffs)

145
00:19:57,932 --> 00:19:59,466
(wind picks up)

146
00:20:02,804 --> 00:20:04,906
Think I'm gonna walk
the long way home.

147
00:20:05,039 --> 00:20:06,339
We'll come with you.

148
00:20:06,974 --> 00:20:08,009
No.

149
00:20:08,576 --> 00:20:10,578
Go on, get that lot
in the freezer.

150
00:20:11,445 --> 00:20:13,213
(footsteps receding rapidly)

151
00:20:15,215 --> 00:20:16,651
(slow dramatic music)

152
00:20:32,166 --> 00:20:34,669
(boat splashing, sloshing,
chugging)

153
00:21:02,196 --> 00:21:03,263
Okay?

154
00:21:05,066 --> 00:21:06,433
They going today?

155
00:21:07,267 --> 00:21:08,870
Still one short.

156
00:21:11,239 --> 00:21:12,540
What you gonna do?

157
00:21:12,907 --> 00:21:13,941
Wait.

158
00:21:15,643 --> 00:21:17,344
We don't go short-handed.

159
00:21:19,847 --> 00:21:20,915
Do we?

160
00:21:27,588 --> 00:21:29,023
Why don't you go, Mike?

161
00:21:30,290 --> 00:21:32,359
I'm a businessman, Tina.

162
00:21:33,094 --> 00:21:34,595
Not a fisherman.

163
00:21:44,437 --> 00:21:46,373
(poignant music)

164
00:21:49,442 --> 00:21:50,878
Can I get an advance?

165
00:21:51,344 --> 00:21:52,814
Advance?

166
00:21:53,047 --> 00:21:54,615
Yeah, just a few quid.

167
00:21:55,950 --> 00:21:58,619
No-one's earnin' 'til
tha's turnin'.

168
00:22:24,477 --> 00:22:25,847
(coin clanks)

169
00:22:27,215 --> 00:22:28,616
(door opens)

170
00:22:30,450 --> 00:22:31,719
Excuse me?

171
00:22:32,553 --> 00:22:33,855
Can I start a tab?

172
00:22:33,955 --> 00:22:34,822
LANDLADY: Sorry pard.

173
00:22:34,922 --> 00:22:35,957
I've got a job.

174
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:37,390
I just ain't been paid yet.

175
00:22:37,490 --> 00:22:38,926
JESS: What's your job?

176
00:22:39,492 --> 00:22:40,828
Fisherman.

177
00:22:41,162 --> 00:22:41,996
Oh yeah?

178
00:22:42,096 --> 00:22:42,997
Deckhand.

179
00:22:44,265 --> 00:22:46,834
I'll get you a drink,
Mr Fisherman.

180
00:22:47,235 --> 00:22:49,570
Thanks.
(soft background music)

181
00:22:52,907 --> 00:22:54,141
Put it on my tab.

182
00:22:54,242 --> 00:22:56,077
You abn' got a tab, Jess.

183
00:22:56,944 --> 00:22:58,112
Can I start one?

184
00:22:58,246 --> 00:22:59,847
No, Jess.

185
00:23:01,414 --> 00:23:03,450
Oh, lend us some money.

186
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:06,854
Charmin'.

187
00:23:07,154 --> 00:23:08,689
My dad was a fisherman.

188
00:23:10,390 --> 00:23:11,826
Wodn'e, Mum?

189
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:16,931
'Cept we don't talk about it.
Do we?

190
00:23:17,031 --> 00:23:18,833
'Ome time idn' it, Jess?

191
00:23:20,201 --> 00:23:21,401
Oh well...

192
00:23:24,639 --> 00:23:26,774
We'll have a drink
when you come back.

193
00:23:27,708 --> 00:23:28,408
Liam.

194
00:23:28,609 --> 00:23:29,944
If you come back.

195
00:23:33,281 --> 00:23:34,882
Now you'll have to come back.

196
00:23:34,982 --> 00:23:35,883
Oh, yeah?

197
00:23:36,317 --> 00:23:37,151
Yeah.

198
00:23:38,185 --> 00:23:39,120
Yeah?

199
00:23:42,390 --> 00:23:44,058
'Cause I want my cap back.

200
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:47,595
(door closes)

201
00:23:51,464 --> 00:23:52,767
Take care out there.

202
00:23:53,433 --> 00:23:54,502
Okay.

203
00:23:56,203 --> 00:23:57,171
Thanks!

204
00:23:57,271 --> 00:23:58,172
(door opens)

205
00:23:59,573 --> 00:24:00,875
(door closes)

206
00:24:00,975 --> 00:24:02,143
(sombre music)

207
00:24:08,182 --> 00:24:09,583
(bird squawking)

208
00:24:14,622 --> 00:24:16,090
(wings fluttering)
(crow caws)

209
00:24:16,190 --> 00:24:18,559
I think they're gonna start
fishing again.

210
00:24:19,327 --> 00:24:20,493
Really?

211
00:24:22,563 --> 00:24:23,597
(crow caws)

212
00:24:24,332 --> 00:24:25,666
(low whooshing)

213
00:24:27,301 --> 00:24:28,803
Summin's goin' on.

214
00:24:29,236 --> 00:24:30,972
(roof caves in)
(loud crash)

215
00:24:31,138 --> 00:24:33,507
(thud)
(rubble crumbling)

216
00:24:42,049 --> 00:24:43,718
(wind blowing outside)

217
00:24:48,422 --> 00:24:50,091
(thunder rumbling)
(heavy rain falling)

218
00:24:56,597 --> 00:24:58,232
(echoing drips)

219
00:24:58,332 --> 00:25:00,201
(dramatic music)

220
00:25:12,246 --> 00:25:13,681
JESS: Oo's boat is it?

221
00:25:14,215 --> 00:25:15,116
TINA: Dunno.

222
00:25:15,616 --> 00:25:16,917
Up the line?

223
00:25:17,985 --> 00:25:19,120
Dunno.

224
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:20,688
Yes, you do.

225
00:25:21,856 --> 00:25:22,857
I don't.

226
00:25:23,024 --> 00:25:23,858
<i>No snow.</i>

227
00:25:23,958 --> 00:25:24,859
You always know.

228
00:25:24,959 --> 00:25:26,761
<i>Should snow for Christmas.</i>

229
00:25:27,828 --> 00:25:29,230
You know everythin'.

230
00:25:31,432 --> 00:25:34,635
Bloody...orifice
of knowledge, you are.

231
00:25:35,536 --> 00:25:36,804
(laughs)

232
00:25:38,839 --> 00:25:39,673
What?

233
00:25:40,775 --> 00:25:42,610
(baby grumbles)

234
00:25:43,010 --> 00:25:45,813
All I know is, it ent goin'
nowhere any time soon.

235
00:25:46,347 --> 00:25:47,415
How come?

236
00:25:47,782 --> 00:25:49,050
They ent got the crew.

237
00:25:50,151 --> 00:25:51,218
They have.

238
00:25:52,653 --> 00:25:53,788
They abn'.

239
00:25:54,455 --> 00:25:56,257
'E looked like crew t'me.

240
00:25:59,060 --> 00:26:00,194
They're one short.

241
00:26:02,663 --> 00:26:04,131
No, they ent.

242
00:26:04,365 --> 00:26:05,666
(baby gurgles)

243
00:26:06,267 --> 00:26:07,735
(dramatic music)

244
00:26:14,041 --> 00:26:15,643
(rustling)

245
00:26:15,843 --> 00:26:17,812
EMILY: We're coming with you.

246
00:26:18,312 --> 00:26:19,914
NICK: I don't want you to come.

247
00:26:20,748 --> 00:26:22,416
We wanna see you off.

248
00:26:22,683 --> 00:26:24,118
I don't want you to.

249
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:27,788
Stay 'ere in the warm.

250
00:26:29,590 --> 00:26:31,158
I'll be back in a coupla days.

251
00:26:32,293 --> 00:26:33,360
I'll be countin'.

252
00:26:37,198 --> 00:26:38,232
See ya.

253
00:26:40,668 --> 00:26:41,802
See ya.

254
00:26:47,741 --> 00:26:49,009
Close the door.

255
00:27:00,254 --> 00:27:01,755
(ominous music)

256
00:27:02,189 --> 00:27:03,958
That boat was lost.

257
00:27:06,694 --> 00:27:08,162
You remember.

258
00:27:09,096 --> 00:27:11,699
She went down short-'anded,
didn' she?

259
00:27:17,238 --> 00:27:18,839
You let 'em down.

260
00:27:21,342 --> 00:27:23,110
You never forgiv'd y'self.

261
00:27:26,147 --> 00:27:28,015
My beautiful boy.

262
00:27:29,551 --> 00:27:30,684
(footsteps receding)

263
00:27:30,784 --> 00:27:32,319
Don't do it to us again.

264
00:27:33,988 --> 00:27:36,724
Me and your dad can't go
through it again.

265
00:28:07,388 --> 00:28:08,923
(poignant music)

266
00:28:09,957 --> 00:28:11,825
(birds twittering)

267
00:28:15,229 --> 00:28:16,363
(door opens)

268
00:28:30,911 --> 00:28:32,880
(waves splashing)

269
00:28:36,016 --> 00:28:38,352
Everyone's be'ind ya, Murgey.

270
00:28:40,287 --> 00:28:41,355
Fair seas.

271
00:28:44,458 --> 00:28:46,126
An' bring the fish back.

272
00:28:50,764 --> 00:28:52,199
(seagulls crying)

273
00:28:55,604 --> 00:28:57,271
(boat rumbling)

274
00:29:00,542 --> 00:29:02,109
(wood clattering)

275
00:29:17,391 --> 00:29:18,759
Alright, my friend?

276
00:29:27,334 --> 00:29:28,435
(bag thunks)

277
00:29:30,904 --> 00:29:32,406
Get the bowline!

278
00:29:35,276 --> 00:29:36,176
MIKE: I got 'n.

279
00:29:54,261 --> 00:29:55,996
(engine roars)

280
00:30:26,093 --> 00:30:28,062
(wake splashes gently)

281
00:30:50,017 --> 00:30:54,154
(boat horn sounding)

282
00:30:59,860 --> 00:31:01,862
(poignant music continues)

283
00:31:27,622 --> 00:31:29,624
See y'soon, m'darlin'.

284
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:34,895
(quiet rumbling)

285
00:32:08,763 --> 00:32:10,431
(sinister music)

286
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:20,441
