01:01:20,948 --> 01:01:23,284
There was some stuff
that needed doing on the boat.

566
01:01:26,053 --> 01:01:27,821
That true, Luke Richards?

567
01:01:33,494 --> 01:01:36,330
You wouldn' tell me though
if it wodn', would yer?

568
01:01:48,142 --> 01:01:50,110
Thick as bleddy shit, you two.

569
01:01:59,820 --> 01:02:01,422
(money rustling)

570
01:02:21,075 --> 01:02:22,076
Thanks.

571
01:02:36,857 --> 01:02:38,225
See you in a few days.

572
01:02:40,662 --> 01:02:41,829
LITTLE JESS: Bye!

573
01:02:49,403 --> 01:02:50,437
Daddy?

574
01:02:53,340 --> 01:02:55,009
You forgot your cap.

575
01:02:59,847 --> 01:03:01,315
(whooshing)

576
01:03:05,919 --> 01:03:07,454
(fish slopping)

577
01:03:07,555 --> 01:03:10,625
MURGEY: Right on! Aah...

578
01:03:10,725 --> 01:03:11,992
Ah...

579
01:03:12,860 --> 01:03:14,295
(boat creaking)

580
01:03:16,797 --> 01:03:18,132
(rhythmic banging)

581
01:03:25,939 --> 01:03:27,274
(seagulls crying)

582
01:03:45,926 --> 01:03:48,028
(clanking, whirring)

583
01:03:49,296 --> 01:03:50,831
(rumbling)

584
01:04:04,612 --> 01:04:05,879
(rhythmic banging continues)

585
01:04:05,979 --> 01:04:07,281
(chains clank)

586
01:04:09,083 --> 01:04:11,051
(boat creaking, straining)

587
01:04:15,055 --> 01:04:16,624
(fish slopping)

588
01:04:22,429 --> 01:04:24,298
(water sloshing)

589
01:04:24,398 --> 01:04:25,466
(sloshing)

590
01:04:27,968 --> 01:04:29,403
(baskets clattering)

591
01:04:31,872 --> 01:04:33,173
(crate scrapes)

592
01:04:34,441 --> 01:04:35,943
(crate bangs)

593
01:04:43,984 --> 01:04:46,954
(rhythmic banging continues)

594
01:04:49,824 --> 01:04:50,991
(seagull squawks)

595
01:04:51,726 --> 01:04:53,026
(cutlery clatters)

596
01:04:53,762 --> 01:04:56,063
Bleddy ansum that was, Decky.

597
01:05:10,545 --> 01:05:11,646
Wha's 'is name?

598
01:05:13,213 --> 01:05:14,214
Wha'?

599
01:05:15,617 --> 01:05:16,518
Him.

600
01:05:18,285 --> 01:05:19,219
Decky.

601
01:05:21,589 --> 01:05:22,690
His real name.

602
01:05:29,864 --> 01:05:31,198
And my real name?

603
01:05:36,905 --> 01:05:38,405
Is Murgey your real name?

604
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:42,109
No.

605
01:05:42,943 --> 01:05:44,344
'Tis a nickname.

606
01:05:45,979 --> 01:05:48,148
Nick. Name. (laughs)

607
01:05:52,085 --> 01:05:53,588
What's your real name?

608
01:05:54,388 --> 01:05:56,724
'Tis lost in the wind, Sir.

609
01:05:59,359 --> 01:06:01,161
That's just the way it is.

610
01:06:05,633 --> 01:06:06,668
Denver?

611
01:06:09,169 --> 01:06:11,940
I may be in charge
of this here vessel,

612
01:06:12,439 --> 01:06:15,409
but that dun't mean I don't
appreciate you boys.

613
01:06:17,978 --> 01:06:19,346
Y' doin' good.

614
01:06:19,881 --> 01:06:22,316
Workin' 'ard
and 'tis much appreciated.

615
01:06:22,584 --> 01:06:25,452
But jus' remember...
for every man at sea,

616
01:06:25,553 --> 01:06:28,121
there's five ashore
relying on yer.

617
01:06:28,222 --> 01:06:29,624
So, stay sharp.

618
01:06:31,793 --> 01:06:32,993
Alright?

619
01:06:34,863 --> 01:06:36,096
(inhales)

620
01:06:37,030 --> 01:06:38,533
(crockery clattering)

621
01:06:39,266 --> 01:06:40,835
How's she lookin' back there?

622
01:06:40,935 --> 01:06:42,369
